---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Access Chudware" description="Open Chudware in a browser with no installation, or ask about native Windows and Linux preview builds.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Browser + native</p>
      <h1>Start in a browser. Install nothing.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The browser client is available now. Create an account to open Chudware in a tab, in your own workspace.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="https://app.chudware.com/signin">Sign in</a></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Available now</p>
        <h2>Full product, running in your tab.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Chudware in the browser is the same application as the desktop build, running in your tab — not a video stream of a machine in a data centre, and not a viewer. The gateway verifies your identity and clamps every file path to your own workspace root.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="pricing-note">
        <p class="eyebrow">No local setup</p>
        <p>Use parametric modeling, assemblies, CAM, PLM, <a class="text-link" href="/product/simulation/">simulation</a>, reverse engineering, and the AI copilot without installing a desktop package. Open STEP, IGES, and BREP solids or STL, OBJ, PLY, and glTF meshes straight from the tab.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Open the signup page <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Native desktop preview</p>
        <h2>Windows and Linux builds exist, but are not publicly published yet.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Native preview access is available on request while the public release channel is being prepared. There are no public artifact links, version numbers, or checksums to publish today.</p>
        <p class="supporting-copy">Both native builds are 64-bit only and need a graphics driver capable of a modern hardware-accelerated 3D context; without one the application does not start. No minimum RAM, CPU, or disk figures are published, because none have been measured and ratified — the browser workspace is the quickest way to find out whether a machine is comfortable.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="platform-grid platform-grid-native">
        <article class="panel platform-card"><p class="eyebrow">Native build</p><h3>Windows</h3><p>Ask about access to the Windows desktop preview.</p><a class="button button-secondary" href="mailto:sales@chudware.com?subject=Windows%20desktop%20preview">Request Windows access</a></article>
        <article class="panel platform-card"><p class="eyebrow">Native build</p><h3>Linux</h3><p>Ask about access to the Linux desktop preview.</p><a class="button button-secondary" href="mailto:sales@chudware.com?subject=Linux%20desktop%20preview">Request Linux access</a></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The shortest route</p>
      <h2>Open Chudware from the browser.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Create an account and start in the browser; no desktop package is required.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Create an account</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/first-part/">Read the first-part guide</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
